<title>USA: U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA wheat export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Net sales of 730,800 metric tons (MT) were two and one-half times the previous week and double the 4-week average.</p>
<p>Pakistan (401,000 MT) was the major buyer. Other significant increases were reported for the Philippines (92,300 MT), Japan (61,500 MT), El Salvador (33,000 MT), and Taiwan (26,400 MT).</p>
<p>Exports of 350,100 MT were 7 percent lower than the week earlier and 4 percent less than the 4-week average.  The principal recipients were Taiwan (86,400 MT), the Philippines (62,300 MT), Venezuela (28,500 MT), Pakistan (21,000 MT), Israel (20,900 MT), and Japan (20,600 MT).</p>
</text>
